## Introduction: The Dome-World Principle

Dome-World is built upon a single, uncompromising structural thesis:

**The best infrastructure does not disappear. It explains itself.**

Water traces its gravitational path. Air reveals its thermal draft. Heat radiates its transfer. Cloth displays its damage. Buildings expose their skeletons.

The settlement becomes a landscape where the physics of survival are not hidden behind drywall or buried beneath asphalt. They are pulled into the light, allowing the patterns of the world to be noticed.

This guide is both a manual for the builder and an ontological grounding for the inhabitant. It documents not just *what* to build, but *why*—and *how* the settlement teaches its own operation to every generation.

