## Chapter 13: The Window‑Which‑Cooks (Solar Engine)

Sunlight is the oldest continuous engine in Dome‑World.

The Window‑Which‑Cooks is an optical device designed to gather and concentrate that radiant energy. It is not a replacement for the base‑load thermal stability of the hõt‑box; it is a high‑grade thermal scavenger, letting photons perform intense work when atmospheric conditions allow.

### The Optical Basket

The Window‑Which‑Cooks extends from the dome’s exterior as a woven parabolic reflector.

Constructed from woven bamboo frames lined with reclaimed aluminum ribbon or polished metals, its geometry is highly engineered. Its sole purpose is to capture scattered sunlight and reflect it into a concentrated, high‑temperature focal point.

### The Focal Chamber

This focal point rests inside a protected thermal chamber. The captured solar radiation creates an intense, localized heat zone capable of boiling water, baking flatbreads, or rapidly dehydrating harvest crops.

The process remains entirely visible. Residents trace the angle of incidence, seeing exactly where the light enters and where the heat gathers.

### The Duties of the Window

The window has one focus and several masters, and it serves them in strict order of need:

| Order | Duty | Timing |
|:---|:---|:---|
| 1 | Generator of cōl‑box absorption loop | Morning (so food keeps) |
| 2 | Midday meal | Peak light (when sun is strongest) |
| 3 | Steam boiler of sanitation corridor | Afternoon (so cleanliness follows) |
| 4 | Toast drawer | Last (scavenging what remains) |

The household allocates the sun’s hours the way it allocates the water: visibly, in turn, by need. The schedule is not a limitation; it is the day’s rhythm made legible.

### Orbital Mechanics (Seasonal Operation)

The Window‑Which‑Cooks demands participation with celestial mechanics.

| Season | Solar Character | Adjustment |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Summer | High‑angle, direct radiation | Steep reflector angle |
| Winter | Low‑angle, diffused light | Shallow reflector angle |

The adjustable supports of the optical basket must be calibrated to the season. The system teaches orbital reality instead of demanding identical, push‑button performance every day of the year.

### Thermal Redundancy

Dome‑World never relies on a single point of failure. When cloud cover prevents optical concentration, the stored masses carry the load:

- Banked ice in the cōl‑box.
- Warm water battery of the hõt‑box.
- Insulated earth.

Sun‑days charge the stores; clouded days spend them. The steam duty waits; the warmth and the cold never stop.

### Learning Through Photons

A child watching the Window‑Which‑Cooks learns fundamental physics:

The sun is kinetic energy. Geometry can redirect that energy. High‑grade heat can be gathered from thin air. The world contains usable power, if you know how to shape the lens.

