## Chapter 14: Living in Dome‑World

A Dome‑World settlement is not defined by its technology. It is defined by how that technology alters human behavior. The purpose of the architecture is not efficiency; it is legibility. It creates a space where people cannot help but notice their relationship to the ecology.

### The Gradual Wake

The day begins with thermodynamics, not alarms. As sunlight strikes the Solar Chimney, the air expands. The draft pulls. Cool air enters the bedroom. The settlement wakes gradually, driven by the changing angle of the sun. There is no single switch that starts the day; the entire metabolism transitions together.

### Maintenance as Participation

In Dome‑World, maintenance is not a chore outsourced to specialists. It is a daily, participatory act. Clearing a water channel, swapping a charcoal filter, harvesting ice from the cold shelf, or tensioning a woven textile is how a resident talks to their house. The work is not an interruption of life. It is the practice of living.

### Kinetic Education

Children learn applied physics through direct interaction:

| Activity | Physics Taught |
|:---|:---|
| Jumping on bedroom bellows | Pneumatic pressure |
| Watching cōl‑box frost | Phase‑change condensation |
| Weaving thread into Binary Loom | Data retention |
| Cranking the fountain | Leverage and fluid dynamics |

Learning is not separated into classrooms; it is embedded in the walls.

### The Social Technology of Food

Meals occur in the à‑place. The food gathers the people. The table is not merely a flat wooden surface; it is a social technology. It organizes time, mandates presence, and centralizes the caloric energy of the household.

### The Metric of Rest (𝄐)

The earth‑sheltered bedroom reminds residents that infrastructure exists to support recovery. The goal of engineering is not maximum continuous output. The goal is achieving enough systemic stability that the inhabitants can safely, deeply pause.

### The Data of Repair

A Dome‑World home expects friction. Membranes tear. Mirrors dull. Weather shifts. Wood ages.

A repaired object is not ruined; a repaired object contains more data than a new one. Visible mending is a form of architectural memory.

### The Ecological Network

The settlement functions through an unbreakable chain of kinetic and caloric exchanges. Water supports transpiration. Transpiration supports plants. Plants support human biology. Humans maintain the mechanics. The mechanics support the rest. Nothing exists independently.

