## Appendix B: Maintenance Philosophy

The prime directive of Dome‑World engineering is visual telemetry.

If a mechanical system cannot be seen, it cannot be understood. If it cannot be understood, it cannot be safely repaired. Obfuscation is the enemy of longevity.

| Principle | Practice |
|:---|:---|
| **Inspect** | Residents perform ambient visual inspections constantly. A dripping valve, a dulled mirror, a slowed draft, a yellowing plant—observation precedes intervention. |
| **Replace** | Components must be modular. When a piece fails, it is unbolted, unstitched, or detached. The damaged module is replaced, and the system continues without missing a breath. |
| **Teach** | Every mechanical failure is an educational opportunity. A child who watches a charcoal panel being swapped or a basin membrane being patched fundamentally understands the system. A person who understands a machine will never be held hostage by it. |

